From 740e1c0df9ab22f5b5ff33f1c0abb60c62b5faab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] book ch.8 (part 1): factorial_anova and nested_anova

Welham et al. (2015) ch. 8.1-8.5: treatment structures.

factorial_anova: crossed structure of 2 or 3 treatment factors with an
optional block (multi-stratum when blocked). Terms for prediction are
chosen by the marginality procedure of Fig. 8.4; predictions are tables
of means for the retained terms with SE and SED from the original ResMS
(no refit, p. 160), LSD, differences with CIs and, for log scales,
ratios. Sum-to-zero effects by inclusion-exclusion of marginal means.
Optional response transformation reuses ch. 6 (log10, ln, sqrt, logit).
Requires each combination equally replicated in every block (orthogonal
case); otherwise an error points to ch. 11.

nested_anova: Group/Member (members may reuse labels across groups),
group and nested SS by RSS differences, nested SS split by group
(Table 8.14), group means with SEDs for unequal sizes, parental and
nested effects; also covers control vs treated (Type/Treatment).

Tests reproduce Tables 8.2, 8.4, 8.5 (beetle, log10), 8.8 and 8.9
(ladybird 2x3x2 in two runs, logit %), 8.22 rows and 8.21 main effects
(herbicide, sqrt), 8.11, 8.12, 8.14 (brassica isolates nested in
species) and 8.15-8.16 (potato control vs fungicides). Book rounding
slips noted in tests: Table 8.5 upper ratio 2.52 (10^0.399 = 2.51),
Table 8.11 A6 nested effect 1.555 (exact 1.556).

Catalog: optional slots (third factor, block); bridge: 'structure' call
kind passing factor columns by name with column names as labels; the
form allows leaving optional slots empty.

